                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "236167257",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197960830998",
                            "num_reviews": 298,
                            "playtime_forever": 17,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 16,
                            "last_played": 1790357096
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The only way to recommend this (if it isn't free or less than .99) is to say it would be great fun for a couple of hours on a Sunday afternoon with a young family (I mean pre high school kids with mum and dad).\n\nOther than that, it feels like a concept game - or a students (very good) project for a video gaming course.\n\nCan't recommend - it's just a kind of angry birds clone where you can fly the bird with your head to get further if you hit it with a perfect swing.\n\nThere are no instructions or guide - so for anyone using Valve index - here's the basic controls:\n\nThere are penguins waiting to dive into a swimming pool, a shop and your character.\n\nYou can teleport by using the thumbstick (hold aim release)\nYou pick up a bat  (trigger button), wait for the penguin to dive and smack him as far as you can, with a swing\nIf you hit him perfectly - you can control him with your head \n\nYou can buy things at the shop (press down on the trackpad)- each time you restart the game you will be given 20,000 credits\n\nThe items in the shop are used when you are controlling the bird , you select them with the trackpad and use them with the trigger button.\n\nEnjoy a bit of daft fun.\n\nBut for me it's 3/10 - I played this 9 years too late , far too basic , wouldn't smack a penguin with a 100t bat again.",
